<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick III of Nuremberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1220–1297</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a> was a Hohenzollern burgrave of Nuremberg who helped secure the election of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-i-of-germany">Rudolf of Habsburg</a> as King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> in 1273. In return Rudolf confirmed his family's hereditary rights. Frederick enlarged the Hohenzollern lands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a>, including the inheritance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayreuth">Bayreuth</a>, laying the foundation of the later margraviates of Ansbach and Bayreuth.</p></div>
